  "question": {
    "text": "How many of the following acids will show higher reactivity towards esterification reaction as compared to acetic acid?<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0033_86b3b677308f.png\" style=\"height: 150px; width: 481px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "The order of reactivity of carboxylic acids towards esterification reaction is, <math><mtext>HCOOH</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mrow><mtext>CH</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>COOH</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mrow><mtext>RCH</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>COOH</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mrow><mtext>R</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mtext>CHCOOH</mtext><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mrow><mtext>R</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mtext>CCOOH</mtext></mrow></msub></math><br />Thus, only methanoic acid will show higher reactivity towards esterification reaction as compared to acetic acid."
  }
}